  "abstract": "Covers the IETF AI Preferences (aipref) working group drafts: the vocabulary for AI usage preferences (draft-ietf-aipref-vocab-08, categories train-ai, ai-use and search, serialized as a Structured Fields Dictionary) and its attachment to HTTP content (draft-ietf-aipref-attach-05, the Content-Usage header field and the robots.txt Content-Usage rule that updates RFC 9309). Both are working group drafts with no RFC, so each is the current line of its own family with a build posture; earlier revisions with breaking label or syntax changes are legacy lines with upgrade checklists. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions and upgrades, the vocabulary and serialization, the attachment mechanisms for publishers, and the processing, combining and limits for crawlers and agents.",
